hadiths[34]{hadithnumber,text}:
"146","“Allah’s Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) did not eat food on a table, nor in a bowl, and no bread rolled thin and flat was baked for him. I asked Qatada: ‘So on\nwhat were they used to eating?’ He said: ‘On these pieces of skin [on which food for the journey is put].”"
"147","“Do you not have what you want in the way of food and drink? I have seen your Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace), and the poor-quality dates  that he finds are what fills his stomach."""""
"148","\Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) did not eat his fill of barley-bread for two days in a row until he died.”"""""
"149","“Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) did not eat food on a table, and he did not eat bread rolled thin and flat, until he died.”"
"150","“Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): ‘What an excellent condiment vinegar is'!”"
"151","“Do you not have what you want in the way of food and drink? I have seen your Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace), and he does not have enough poor-quality dates (daqal) to fill his stomach.\""152"""""
"152","Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Khuzai narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""What an excellent condiment is vinegar."""""
"153","\We were in the presence of Abu Musa al- Ash'ari when he was brought some chicken meat. A man among the people thereupon turned away"
"154","\I ate together with Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) the meat of a bustard.”"""""
"155","\We were in the presence of Abu Musa al-Ash'ari. Among the people there was a man from the Banu Taimi’llah"
"156","“Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): ‘Eat [olive] oil, and anoint with it, for it is from a blessed tree!’”"
"157","“Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): ‘Eat oil, and anoint with it, for it is from a blessed tree'!”"
"158","Another chain reports similar to the previous narration and it did not mention \related from 'Umar (RA)\"""""""
"159","“The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to admire the gourd, so when he was brought a meal or invited to one, I would seek it out and set it in front of him, because I knew that he liked it.”"
"160","\I entered the presence of the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace)"
"161","“A tailor invited Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) to a meal he had made, so I went with Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) to that meal. He presented Allah's Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) with some barley-bread and broth containing a gourd and jerked meat. Then I saw the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) looking for chunks of gourd all around the bowl, and and I've loved gourd ever since.”"
"162","\The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to love sweets and honey.”"""""
"163","Umm Salama informed 'Ata ibn Yasar that she served Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) a grilled flank, so he ate from it, then embarked on the ritual prayer and did not perform the minor ritual ablution."
"164","\Together with Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace)"
"165","“I was a guest one night together with Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace), so he was brought a grilled flank. Then he took the blade and set about carving, and he carved some for me. Bilal arrived calling him to prayer, so he threw the blade away, and he said: ‘Why have his hands been soiled?’ His mustache hung down close to his mouth, so he said to him: ‘I shall clip it for you over a tooth-stick,’ or: ‘Clip it over a tooth-stick'!”"
"166","‘The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) was brought some meat, so the foreleg was set before him, and he liked it, so he took a bite of it.”"
"167","\The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to like the foreleg [of the cooked sheep].\"" He [Ibn Mas'ud] also said: \""He was poisoned with a foreleg"
"168","\I cooked a dish for the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace)"
"169","“The foreleg was not the meat dearest to Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace), but he only got to have meat occasionally, so he would rush to it, because it was the part that got done the most quickly.”"
"170","“I heard Allah’s Messenger say (Allah bless him and give him peace): ‘The best of the meat is the back'.”"
"171","\The Prophet said (Allah bless him and give him peace): 'What an excellent condiment vinegar is'!”"""""
"172","\The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) entered my presence and said: 'Do you have anything in your possession?' I said: 'No"
"173","“The superiority of 'Aisha over all other women is like the superiority of tharid [a dish of sopped bread, meat and broth] over all other food.”"
"174","“Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace):‘The superiority of 'A'isha over all other women is like the superiority of tharid [a dish of sopped bread, meat and broth] over all other food'.”"
"175","Abu Huraira (may Allah be well pleased with him) said that he saw Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) perform the minor ritual ablution because of eating cottage cheese. Then he saw him eat from the flank of a sheep, and then perform the ritual prayer without performing the minor ritual ablution."
"176","\Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) gave a wedding banquet for Safiyya consisting of dried dates and parched barley.”"""""
"177","\Make us a meal consisting of that which used to delight Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace)"
"178","“The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) came to us in our house, so we slaughtered a sheep for him, and he said: ‘It is as if they knew that we love meat'!\ (This\ntradition is part of a longer story)."""""
"179","“Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) went out and I went with him, then he went in to see a woman from among the Helpers [al-Ansar], so she slaughtered a sheep for him and he ate some of it. She also brought him a dish of ripe dates, and he ate some of them. Then he performed the minor ritual ablution for the noon prayer, and performed it. Then he departed, and she\nbrought him a leftover from the remnant of the sheep, and he ate. Then he performed the afternoon ritual prayer but did not perform the minor ritual ablution.”"
